    description: "Found by the 2026-11-15 review of the stable-id items (reports and fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026). Re-run by hand the same day at dev e2b6ab8096, analyzer 9.2.0.\n\nDEFECT (stale reason text that is read as a blocker). packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_doc_family_id_parity.py:\nthe module docstring (lines 60-68) says the KIND_SLOT_HOLES residuals are \"stable_id-scheme-gated ... sequenced\nbehind WI-talos v9/v10\", and the `robot` entry of KIND_SLOT_HOLES (lines 318-327) says \"scheme-gated behind\nWI-talos v9/v10, the same gate WI-banod T1 waits on\". INV-kurup-tidam-ribus-rorif-jigad-tijah-losus-funah's last discussion entry repeats it.\n\nWHAT IS TRUE TODAY. v9 shipped on 2026-10-13 as the WI-tusad bump and v10 on 2026-10-22 as the WI-banod T1 fix;\nneither was the WI-talos relabel, which has not shipped. dev is at stableid-v14 and v10-v14 are unreleased (the\nlast release, v9.2.0, carries v9). WI-banod T1 is done. Five scheme bumps have shipped since the text was written\nand none picked up the robot fix.\n\nWhat does still hold: the `kind` argument to make_doc_symbol_ids feeds make_doc_stable_id, so correcting robot's\nword changes those symbols' stable ids, and by the owner's rule (an input change to the hash is a scheme bump) the\nfix needs a bump. It needs A bump; it does not wait behind WI-talos.\n\nASK. Rewrite both passages to say that, and name INV-dulah-kisiz-gobak-jafov-soduj-tomim-dufut-kinil limb 1 as the item that carries the robot fix, so the next\nscheme bump is told to include it.\n\nACCEPTANCE. Neither passage names a gate that has cleared; the strict xfail for robot still XPASSes when the kind\nword is corrected.\n\nNOT CHECKED: other docstrings or comments citing the v9/v10 gate (ADR-0051:181-186 does; that one is recorded on\nthe module-key item)."  # c0f0
